                <h3 class="postingHeader">Job Description and Duties</h3>
                <p class="postingContent">
                    <p style="font-family: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="color: #333333;">The Department of State Hospitals-Napa, Personnel Office is recruiting to fill a&nbsp;</span>permanent, full-time<span style="color: #333333;"> Personnel Supervisor II. Applicants will be&nbsp;<span style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; text-align: left;">responsible to plan, organize and direct the work of the personnel transactions team and process the most complex documents and transactions. Hires, supervises, trains and audits the work of one Personnel Supervisor I, and multiple&nbsp;Personnel Specialists and Senior Personnel Specialists who are responsible for&nbsp;processing employee transactions including, but not limited to, payroll, leave accounting, garnishments, collections on over payments, and additional duties. Acts as a resource to management throughout the hospital regarding personnel matters.</span></span><br /></span></span><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;"><br /><strong>Per CalHR, the&nbsp;Personnel Supervisor II&nbsp;position is eligible for an annual payment up to&nbsp;$4,800, payable upon meeting the designated criteria as stated in <a href="https://gcc02.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.calhr.ca.gov%2FPay%2520Differentials%2520Library%2FPay_Differential_240.pdf%23search%3Dpersonnel%2520specialist&amp;data=05%7C01%7CTeresita.Oracion%40dsh.ca.gov%7C5329af6223854c0b6f8908db62d4c782%7C807536a6a6b14893a01370509c59ebbb%7C0%7C0%7C638212438281811930%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C3000%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=Y7UVorwtoHWpQlPu%2BZl56sZhSVvzDodH11a9hDGfvsQ%3D&amp;reserved=0" style="text-decoration-line: none;"><span style="color: #0563c1; text-decoration-line: underline;">Pay Differential 240</span></a></strong></span><strong><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;"> .<br /><br /> </span></strong><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><strong><a name="_Hlk92277833" style="box-sizing: border-box; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial; font-family: Arial;"><span style="box-sizing: border-box;">This advertisement will run &quot;until filled&quot; with a cutoff date for review on the 16th of each month.</span></a></strong></span></p><p style="font-family: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><strong><span style="font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt;"> </span></strong><span style="font-size: 12pt;">All interested qualified applicants that <strong>meet the minimum qualifications, see link below</strong>,&nbsp;are encouraged to apply via CalCareers.&nbsp;</span><span style="font-size: 12pt;">To ensure that your application will be considered for this recruitment the following items are required:</span></p><ul type="disc"><li style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif; margin-bottom: 10pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">You are required to pass the Personnel Supervisor II examination, located at&nbsp;<a href="https://www.calcareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/Exams/Bulletin.aspx?examCD=1PB12"></a><a href="https://calcareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/Exams/ExamBulletin.aspx?ExamControlId=1987">Personnel Supervisor II Exam</a>&nbsp;on the CalCareers web site or have current/previous transfer eligibility into the classification.</span></li><li style="font-family: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Include in the&nbsp;JOB TITLE(S)&nbsp;section of the application<strong>&nbsp;&quot;</strong><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">PERSONNEL SUPERVISOR II, JC-460861</span></strong>”.</span></li></ul><div><span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"></span></div><ul type="disc"><li style="font-family: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Complete      the STD 678 EMPLOYMENT APPLICATION in its entirety. Include d</span><span style="font-size: 12pt;">uties performed, supervisor’s name and employment contact information on the STD 678.&nbsp;<strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Incomplete applications will be screened out.</span></strong>&nbsp;</span></li></ul><div><span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"></span></div><ul type="disc"><li style="font-family: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Resumes      will not be accepted in lieu of information required&nbsp;on the STD&nbsp;678 to meet the minimum qualifications.</span></li></ul><div><span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"></span></div><ul type="disc"><li style="font-family: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Foreign      transcripts must be evaluated&nbsp;and submitted with your application,&nbsp;</span><p style="margin: 0pt 0pt 8pt; line-height: 1.07917;"><span style="font-family: Calibri; font-size: 11pt;"><a href="https://www.ctc.ca.gov/credentials/leaflets/foreign-transcript-evaluation-(cl-635)#:~:text=Individuals%20who%20have%20completed%20college%20or%20university%20course,Commission%20for%20a%20California%20credential%2C%20permit%2C%20or%20certificate." style="font-size: 11pt; text-decoration: none;"><span style="color: #0000ff; font-family: Arial; font-size: 12pt; text-decoration: underline;">Foreign Transcript Evaluation (CL-635) (ca.gov)</span></a>&nbsp;.</span></p></li><li style="font-family: &quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Education      required to meet the minimum qualifications will require proof of degree      and/or transcript submitted with application STD&nbsp;678.</span></li></ul><div><p><span style="font-size: 12pt;"></span></p></div><p>You will find additional information about the job in the <strong><a href='https://www.CalCareers.ca.gov/CalHrPublic/FileDownload.aspx?aid=25941664&name=PersonnelSupervisorII02-2